> Would it make sense to use a session-scoped config as the canonical instance and have function-scoped configs operate on copies of it?

It does, however this is out of scope of this PR. 

I actually tried doing this and found that we have the same issue that we had with `TerminalImportMixin`. On the other hand, since `self.config` is used within `setup_beets`, we don't have much other choice but to continue using `config` attribute:

```py
    @cached_property
    def config(self) -> beets.IncludeLazyConfig:
        return self.request.getfixturevalue("config")
```

@snejus I also realized there is some code duplication we can refactor, and that we can fix the position-trusting bug you highlighted earlier across the plugin. Let me know if you would prefer that. 

edit: I went ahead and refactored the code to simplify the plugin and remove the dead/duplicate code in 
314b059. I can revert that if you prefer not to.

I see it now (it is a different bug): the problem is your `albumfields` config is incorrect and includes item-only fields like track, title, path, and catalognum alongside genuine album fields (album, year, country, etc.). The plugin never validates that `albumfields` only contains genuinely album-level fields. 

I updated the plugin to restrict `_importer_edit_album_header` to a known-safe allowlist of true album-level fields (ignoring anything not actually on the `Album` model, or anything that isn't part of `AlbumMatch`). 

@snejus Please try your query now.
